From: =?UTF-8?q?L=C3=A9onard?= <leonard@synthe.se>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:52:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 101/104] net: bcmgenet: Poll the internal PHY on GENET v2

Local workaround, not for upstream as is: on the BCM7231 (GENET v2) no
link change interrupt reached the MAC, so the link never came up with
PHY_MAC_INTERRUPT. Poll the PHY there, as on GENET v5.

The root cause is not known. Whether it is still needed since the
device tree got the BCM7231 interrupt numbers right (the vendor's are
the L1 bit + 1) has not been checked.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmmii.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmmii.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmmii.c
index 0f0dbab..e5ea816 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmmii.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmmii.c
@@ -401,9 +401,10 @@ int bcmgenet_mii_probe(struct net_device *dev)
 	 * Ethernet MAC ISRs. On GENETv5 there is a hardware issue
 	 * that prevents the signaling of link UP interrupts when
 	 * the link operates at 10Mbps, so fallback to polling for
-	 * those versions of GENET.
+	 * those versions of GENET. No link interrupt reaches the MAC on the
+	 * GENETv2 of the BCM7231 either: poll there too.
 	 */
-	if (priv->internal_phy && !GENET_IS_V5(priv))
+	if (priv->internal_phy && !GENET_IS_V5(priv) && !GENET_IS_V2(priv))
 		dev->phydev->irq = PHY_MAC_INTERRUPT;
 
 	/* Indicate that the MAC is responsible for PHY PM */
